    <abstract id="aspace_17781aa384bfc6fc01b40d80c37ff417">Claire O'Connor (d. 2011) was the head publicist and Director of Operations for the Limelight nightclub chain during the 1980s and 1990s. The Claire O'Connor Papers (dated 1965-2010) documents the professional life of O'Connor, focusing heavily on her career in public relations at the Limelight nightclubs in New York and London from the mid-1980s through the 1990s. The collection contains club ephemera; diaries detailing club operations and her address book; photographs of club events, notable guests, and interior and exterior venue shots; drafts and proposals related to her unpublished book, <emph render="italic">Lying with Dogs: Inside the Limelight Nightclub</emph>; and  correspondence with Limelight owner, Peter Gatien. The collection also contains press coverage from 1987 to 1997 that documents the club's legal troubles and a small portion of personal ephemera related to rock musician, Adam Bomb, O'Connor's husband until her death in 2011.</abstract>
